		{
			"id": "en2VU3QBnFC7NrMny",
			"description": "'Eavy Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 7: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 7 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nRigid, riveted plate over a padded underlayer; imposes the usual GURPS bulky-armour DX/Stealth penalties for rigid heavy armour, on top of which most 'Eavy Armour is loud, mismatched and covered in Ork decoration that does the wearer's Stealth no additional favours (GM's discretion on a further penalty for a particularly garish suit).\n\nLore: Standard-issue heavy plate for veteran Boyz and Nobz: welded and riveted metal plate, thick enough to shrug off small-arms fire, worn openly as a mark of status as much as protection. Codex: Orks background and Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos both place it clearly above the scrap armour worn by lesser Boyz and clearly below a Meganob's mega armour.\n\nDesign: Matches the framework's Ork anchor exactly (\"'Eavy armour | Torso DR 45, Weak Points 7\"). Exact dice distribution against the Imperium weapon anchors: a lasgun (7d(2) burn) penetrates 66.8% of the time - 'Eavy Armour is not remotely las-proof the way Astartes plate is - an autogun (7d pi, no divisor) penetrates 0% of the time - it stops solid slugs outright, matching the framework's general \"flak/carapace-class armour stops stub rounds\" logic at a scrap-built DR 45 - and a bolter (6dx2(2) pi++) penetrates 99.0% of the time, confirming that a boltgun shreds even an Ork's best rigid plate almost every time, exactly the one-sided matchup every piece of Astartes-vs-Ork fiction depicts. Limb/head DR use the same proportional offsets as the project's other rigid-plate entries (roughly torso x0.75-0.9 for limbs and head, torso x0.75 for the eye slit, the framework's three-quarters-of-helmet eye-lens rule), and the eye DR (30) is three-quarters of the helmet's 40 like every other suit. Weight 45 lb, heavier for its DR than any comparable Imperium armour (Guard carapace is DR 70 at 30 lb) - Ork armour is thick and crude rather than efficiently engineered, trading weight for the DR it does deliver.",
