		{
			"id": "eucr5yl7YUcy2cMQZ",
			"description": "Mega Armour",
			"local_notes": "Weak Points 6: when a hit on this armour fails to penetrate, roll 3d; on 6 or less it found a gap and DR is halved against it.\n\nServo-assisted plate, worn almost exclusively by Meganobz; imposes rigid heavy armour DX/Stealth penalties as any suit this bulky would, and -3 to Basic Move while worn for its sheer mass: a Meganob's unarmoured Move 9 drops to about 6 in the suit. The figure is a house call, not a Codex number, since no source gives Mega Armour a consistent mobility figure the way it does for Gravis and Terminator suits; servo-assisted strength keeps it from being worse.\n\nLore: The Ork answer to Terminator plate: a massive, welded suit of servo- assisted armour built almost entirely by hand for a single Meganob, thick enough to shrug off small-arms and bolter fire and strong enough to swing a power klaw one-handed. The framework's own anchor table cites it by name as \"an Ork answer to Terminator plate,\" and Codex: Orks background consistently shows Meganobz wading through the kind of fire that would kill an ordinary Boy outright.\n\nDesign: Matches the framework's Ork anchor exactly (\"Mega armour | Torso DR 150, Weak Points 6: an Ork answer to Terminator plate\"). Exact dice distribution: a bolter (6dx2(2) pi++) penetrates 0% of the time and even a heavy bolter ((8d+2)x2(2) pi++) only 6% - Mega Armour is effectively bolter-proof, matching the Terminator-tier role the anchor names directly - while a lascannon (8dx8(5) burn, 100%), krak missile (6dx6(5) cr, 100%) and a power fist at Astartes strength (thr+8d(10) cr, 99.99%) all still go through reliably, the same \"only real anti-armour or anti-Terminator weapons beat this\" profile the Imperium's own Terminator plate carries. Weak Points 6 (worse - gappier - than the Imperium Terminator's own WP 3) is taken directly from the anchor and encodes exactly what \"Ork answer to\" should mean mechanically: comparable raw DR, meaningfully worse fit and finish, so massed fire finds the welded seams of a hand-built Ork suit far more often than the mass-produced, black-carapace-fitted plate of a Space Marine. Limb/head DR scale from the torso figure using the same proportions this project's Imperium Terminator entries use (roughly x0.875 for limbs, x0.75 for face, x0.69 for neck); eye DR (112, three-quarters of the helmet's 150) sits below the Imperium Terminator's 150 because the helmet is lower (150 against 200), reflecting cruder construction at comparable bulk. Servo ST (lifting_st 15, striking_st 8) is set below the Imperium Terminator suit's own servo bonus (lifting 20, striking 10) for the same \"comparable but cruder\" reasoning, while still being what actually lets a Meganob swing a power klaw or killsaw one-handed. Weight 220 lb matches the Imperium's Gravis (220 lb) and is below full Terminator plate (300-340 lb), reasoned as \"as heavy as the most armoured non-Terminator human-scale suit, for a smaller (if far stronger) wearer than an Astartes.\" TL 11 like the Imperial Terminator plate it answers (framework TL table: power armour 11); Meks build it by instinct, so Mek Instinct offsets the TL penalty for them.",
