		{
			"id": "eA30U9fpevoiDceAK",
			"description": "Bosspole",
			"local_notes": "A Nob or Boss carrying a bosspole into a mob adds +1 to his own Leadership-equivalent rolls to keep that mob fighting (GM's discretion on the exact roll used, per whatever leadership/morale rules the campaign runs) - Ork mobs rally, or get beaten back into line, at the sight and sound of the pole as much as at the Boss's voice.\n\nLore: A tall pole topped with trophies, totems, the skulls of the Boss's defeated rivals, and (in Ork Freebooter and Speed Freek variants) an assortment of scrap-metal decoration, carried by any Nob or Warboss who leads a mob; Codex: Orks background is explicit that a bosspole is as much a rallying standard as it is a club for beating faltering Boyz back into the fight, and it is rarely put down even when its owner has a choppa or klaw in the other hand.\n\nDesign: Not a framework anchor; built as a plain, long-hafted club (sw+1 cr, reach 1, parry 0U, Axe/Mace - the same baseline the Imperium Guardsman's Club uses) since nothing in the lore suggests a bosspole out-hits an ordinary length of decorated wood and scrap in a fight, with its real value represented as a flat Leadership-style bonus per the \"rallying standard\" half of its description rather than as extra damage - the same design choice this project makes for the Imperium Commissar's Sabre, whose value is largely symbolic and social rather than mechanical. Handling: 8 lb (heavier than the Guardsman's Club for the trophies and decoration bolted to it), min ST 10, ordinary for any Ork.",
